## Traceability Assessment

**Are all acceptance criteria traceable to at least one test case?**

✅ Yes. All documented acceptance criteria (AC-1, AC-2, AC-2.1, AC-2.2) are traceable to one
or more manual test cases.

### Gaps / Clarifications Identified

| Gap ID | Description | Related Test Case |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **GAP-1** | Acceptance criteria state that State D claims move to Expired status, but do not define whether Expired claims can be edited, updated, or submitted. | MW-2170-TC-007 |
| **GAP-2** | Acceptance criteria define behavior for today < DATE+60 and today > DATE+60, but not today = DATE+60. Boundary behavior is undefined. | MW-2170-TC-008 |

## Risk Summary

- **High Risk:** TC-001 through TC-006 — they validate compliance-driven program eligibility,
  reassignment logic, claim status transitions, and prevention of invalid claim processing.
- **Medium Risk:** TC-007 and TC-008 — they identify requirement ambiguities rather than
  validating implemented business logic.

**Overall Traceability Status:** ✅ Complete coverage, with two documented requirement
ambiguities requiring business clarification before final signoff.
